.TH "AUTOBOT" "1" "2026" "reproctl" "Repro Development Tools"
.SH NAME
autobot \- public queue interface for queued work items
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]autobot\f[R] \f[I]subcommand\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Autobot is the repo\-owned public queue CLI for work items.
It uses queue/item language rather than internal claim/run terminology
and is intended to be run from the main checkout.
.PP
The queue is managed locally and the standalone engine performs work
item handoff from queued to prepared delivery state.
.PP
JSON responses are versioned with \f[CR]schema_version: 1\f[R].
Public status\-oriented commands also include a \f[CR]config\f[R] block
sourced from \f[CR].autobot/config.json\f[R].
Current config keys include \f[CR]engine.auto\-discover\f[R],
\f[CR]engine.queue\-depth\f[R], and \f[CR]engine.max\-concurrency\f[R].
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\f[B]add\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]]
Queue an issue for delivery without creating a worktree.
.TP
\f[B]remove\f[R] \f[I]issue\f[R] [\f[B]\-f\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]]
Remove a queued item and restore its Linear assignment/state where
possible.
.TP
\f[B]list\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Show non\-terminal queued items.
.TP
\f[B]status\f[R] [\f[I]\f[R]issue\f[I]\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Show queue summary, or a single item when an issue identifier is
supplied.
.TP
\f[B]logs\f[R] [\f[I]\f[R]issue\f[I]\f[R]] [\f[B]\-t\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Inspect engine or issue logs.
.TP
\f[B]discover\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-limit\f[R] \f[I]N\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-project\f[R] \f[I]name\f[R]] [\f[B]\-q\f[R]] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Reuse the discovery pipeline and print queued issue identifiers.
.TP
\f[B]config get\f[R] \f[I]key\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Read a repo\-scoped Autobot setting.
.TP
\f[B]config set\f[R] \f[I]key\f[R] \f[I]value\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Persist a repo\-scoped Autobot setting.
.TP
\f[B]config unset\f[R] \f[I]key\f[R] [\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]]
Remove a repo\-scoped Autobot setting override.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-json\f[R]
Emit machine\-readable JSON instead of human text.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dry\-run\f[R]
Show the action without mutating local state or Linear.
.TP
\f[B]\-f\f[R]
Force removal of in\-flight work.
.TP
\f[B]\-q\f[R]
Print only issue identifiers, one per line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
autobot add REP\-123
Queue a work item.
.TP
autobot list \-\-json
Inspect the current queue as JSON.
.TP
autobot discover \-q | xargs autobot add
Pipe discovered work directly into the queue.
.TP
autobot config set engine.auto\-discover on
Enable engine\-driven intake for the current repository.
.TP
autobot config list \-\-json
Inspect the repo\-scoped config surface as JSON.
